??My uncle discovered the secret of why he was called Bunny in school until the tenth grade. In the first grade, before the New Year's matinee, it turned out that he could not sing, dance, too, and forgot the poems from the horror of the audience. And the teacher found him a role. He was supposed to jump around the Christmas tree like a rabbit after the rhyme about the bunny. He tells me.

"My mother made me a suit: erect ears, a fluffy tail on his pants, even white gloves were found. A poem about a bunny read, I jump out 
